        "problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(w-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=w$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(w-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061w\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061w\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061w\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061w\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061w-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061w).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
